296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 167 0 R
/T (The top-scoring candidates from beam and evolutionary search are ranked by regularised validation score. The top k rich-class candidates, together with the exhaustive reference winner, are advanced to a finalist pool for repeated held-out evaluation, where k is a predefined finalist count.)
/E (The top-scoring candidates from beam and evolutionary search are ranked by regularised validation score. The top k rich-class candidates, together with the exhaustive reference winner, are advanced to a finalist pool for repeated held-out evaluation, where k is a predefined finalist count.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Repeated test evaluation: Each finalist is independently re-trained and evaluated on the 5 test environments \(games\) across finalist repeats different random seeds. This re-training is fresh each time, no weights are carried over. The candidate with lowest mean repeated test loss across all seeds becomes the final selected utility function.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
