342 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 172 0 R
/T (Agent convergence: The dominant early problem was that DQN agents were nowhere near convergence when moments were scored. With epsilon decay = 4000 and 120 training episodes, agents were 79% random. Behavioral moments from a nearly-random policy carry no utility-relevant signal, they reflect exploration noise rather than preference-driven choice. )
/E (Agent convergence: The dominant early problem was that DQN agents were nowhere near convergence when moments were scored. With epsilon decay = 4000 and 120 training episodes, agents were 79% random. Behavioral moments from a nearly-random policy carry no utility-relevant signal, they reflect exploration noise rather than preference-driven choice. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
