351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (The central scientific observation is that the methodology succeeds when the target utility function produces behavioural moments that are genuinely discriminative across the game environments used for candidate selection. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 767 0 R
/E (With altruism weight = 0.35, the social tradeoff utility prescribes the same optimal actions as a selfish utility in dictator, ultimatum, and the public goods game: the validation environments produce near-identical moments regardless of which utility is being evaluated, making recovery impossible in principle. Raising altruism weight to 1.0 crosses the threshold at which the social utility prescribes qualitatively different optimal behaviour in those same environments, and the benchmark immediately recovers the correct utility structure with 100% win rate and significance against the full finalist field. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (This demonstrates that the pipeline itself is sound: the RL training, moment extraction, search methods, and selection procedure all function as intended, and that the binding constraint on recovery is not computational but informational: the game environments used for validation must be chosen, and the target utility parameterised, such that different utility hypotheses generate observationally distinct behavioural signatures in those environments.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
