358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The results provide proof of concept for the proposed methodology. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The abstract argues that utility function construction, while inherently subjective, can be systematically informed by empirical data, in the same way that Fehr-Schmidt drew on ultimatum game experiments to calibrate the relative weights of selfishness and altruism. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
360 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The benchmark operationalises this directly: agents are trained under candidate utility specifications and their resulting behaviour is compared against a behavioural target, with the specification that best predicts observed behaviour selected as the recovered utility function. The successful recovery is algebraically equivalent to the true social tradeoff utility, with full significance against all comparators and a 100% win rate across repeated evaluations, demonstrates that the proposed AI-driven pipeline can identify the correct balance of selfishness and altruism from behavioural data alone, without requiring  he researcher to specify that balance in advance.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The benchmark progression further validates the proposal's framing of this as a scalable and rigorous methodology. The two-stage selection procedure: complexity-penalised search followed by repeated held-out evaluation with formal significance testing. Ablations will also be provided in the final papper.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
362 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 174 0 R
/E (The finding that all three search methods independently converged on the social component of the utility as the dominant predictive signal, and that the result held across 20 independent repeated evaluations, is robust with regards to the rapid development of optimal utility functions from real world data. )
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
